    "narrative": "The core of our lineup today is anchored by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, who provides the highest utility at 76.75 against the lefty Matthew Liberatore; he is an essential play given his strong park factor and favorable platoon split. We are also leaning heavily into the matchup against the struggling JR Ritchie, which boosts **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (71.49) and **Nasim Nunez** (61.86) into viable starting territory. While **Gunnar Henderson** faces an elite arm in Zack Wheeler, his projection holds firm at 67.14, buoyed significantly by a high park factor and a platoon advantage that keeps him in the optimal slot despite the 41% rain risk in Philadelphia.\n\nTactically, the most difficult decision involved our bench, where **Jorge Polanco** (49.12) narrowly missed the final cut behind **Luis Robert Jr.** (51.38). While **Luis Robert Jr.** struggles against right-handed pitching\u2014evidenced by his -15% dynamic platoon adjustment\u2014his raw power upside against a high-ERA matchup kept him in the lineup over **Jorge Polanco**, whose value was depressed by a poor batting order position. We are closely monitoring **Gunnar Henderson** and the rain threat, as well as the status of **Drake Baldwin**, **Liam Hicks**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Kyle Tucker**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Andy Pages**, and **Heliot Ramos**, all of whom are currently projected based on assumed lineup positions. Should any of these players be relegated to the bottom of the order once official lineups are posted, we will reassess our efficiency thresholds to protect our game caps.",
